<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal inflation to fall more quickly from April.</title>
<headline>Portugal inflation to fall more quickly from April.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese inflation will fall more quickly from April, the Bank of Portugal said in its latest monthly report.</p>
<p>&quot;The trend of disinflation will be more noticeable from April,&quot; it said.  </p>
<p>The Portuguese government has set a target for inflation of between 2.25 and 2.50 percent in 1997.</p>
